{
  "format": "paseo-canvas-pack",
  "version": 1,
  "id": "title-case",
  "name": "Title Case",
  "description": "Gives the selected cards titles in Title Case.",
  "blockTypes": [],
  "templates": [],
  "documents": [],
  "extensions": [
    {
      "id": "title-case.title-case",
      "kind": "tool",
      "api": 1,
      "name": "Title Case",
      "description": "Gives the selected cards titles in Title Case.",
      "icon": "CaseSensitive",
      "permissions": [
        "edit"
      ],
      "html": "<style>body{margin:0;padding:12px;font:13px system-ui,sans-serif}button{font:inherit;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid;cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}</style>\n<p id=\"info\">Select some cards.</p>\n<button id=\"go\" disabled>Title Case the titles</button>\n<script data-lienzo=\"actions\">\n// The work, once: the button below runs it, and so can an agent (canvas_extension_run), headless, without this page.\nfunction titleCase(t) { return t.replace(/\\b\\w/g, function (c) { return c.toUpperCase(); }); }\nlienzo.action('titleCase', function (input, c) {\n  var ids = input.ids || c.selection;\n  var ops = c.document.blocks.filter(function (b) { return ids.indexOf(b.id) >= 0 && titleCase(b.title) !== b.title; })\n    .slice(0, 200).map(function (b) { return { type: 'block.update', id: b.id, patch: { title: titleCase(b.title) } }; });\n  if (!ops.length) return { changed: 0 };\n  return lienzo.edit(ops, 'Title Case').then(function () { return { changed: ops.length }; });\n});\n</script>\n<script>\nvar info = document.getElementById('info'), go = document.getElementById('go');\nlienzo.onContext(function (c) {\n  var k = c.theme.colors, n = c.document.blocks.filter(function (b) { return c.selection.indexOf(b.id) >= 0; }).length;\n  document.body.style.background = k.surface; document.body.style.color = k.foreground;\n  go.style.background = k.accent; go.style.color = k.background; go.style.borderColor = k.accent;\n  info.textContent = n ? n + ' selected' : 'Select some cards.';\n  go.disabled = !n;\n});\ngo.onclick = function () {\n  lienzo.run('titleCase', {}).then(function (r) { info.textContent = r.changed ? 'Done. Undo brings the old titles back.' : 'They are in Title Case already.'; }, function (e) { info.textContent = e.message; });\n};\n</script>",
      "docs": "Title Case gives every selected card a title in Title Case, in one step you can undo.\n\n## Use it\n\n1. Select the cards to tidy.\n2. Open **Title Case** from the + catalog (Extensions).\n3. Press **Title Case the titles**.\n\n> It needs the \"Changes the canvas\" permission. Undo (⌘Z) brings the old titles back.\n\n## Ask your agent\n\nYour agent can run it too: \"Title Case the cards I selected\" or \"Title Case the titles of the cards in this Frame\". Its change shows in History as **Title Case (agent)** and undoes like any other.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "name": "titleCase",
          "description": "Rewrites card titles in Title Case, in one undoable edit. Without ids it works on the cards the person selected.",
          "input": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "ids": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "maxItems": 200,
                "description": "The cards to change. Default: the person's selection."
              }
            }
          },
          "returns": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "changed": {
                "type": "integer",
                "description": "How many titles changed."
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}